Proposal (lane RELEASE): let hosted CI run lane RELEASE's own tests.

Not applied: tools/ci_gate.py is frozen; only Lucas applies this, by his hand or his
word. Apply from the repository root, after the change that adds tools/release/:

    git apply --check tools/release/proposals/ci-gate-release-tests.patch
    git apply --index tools/release/proposals/ci-gate-release-tests.patch

Why: the frozen gate fails on a file named test_*.py outside its globs, and
tools/release/ is not among them, so the lane's tests are named *_checks.py and the
gate does not run them. Without this patch nothing in hosted CI fails on an unpinned
or unhashed line in requirements-ci.txt (the lane's brief asks for that test).

What it does:
- tools/ci_gate.py: adds "tools/release/test_*.py" to TEST_GLOBS;
- renames tools/release/hash_lock_checks.py to tools/release/test_hash_lock.py and
  tools/release/proposal_checks.py to tools/release/test_proposals.py, unchanged.
After it, the gate runs both files on Linux, Windows and macOS.

diff --git a/tools/ci_gate.py b/tools/ci_gate.py
index c98bd2f30d3e5956df17def69a7c1aebc57d9776..b8ec09005f0a23beee4ddfb9508f79d9281c8754 100644
--- a/tools/ci_gate.py
+++ b/tools/ci_gate.py
@@ -60,6 +60,7 @@ TEST_GLOBS = (
     "experiments/**/*_tests.py",
     "experiments/**/*.test.py",
     "core/**/test_*.py",
+    "tools/release/test_*.py",
 )

 # The rebuilt core (CSL-795, PRODUCT.md A19/A38). Its tests import the package
diff --git a/tools/release/hash_lock_checks.py b/tools/release/test_hash_lock.py
similarity index 100%
rename from tools/release/hash_lock_checks.py
rename to tools/release/test_hash_lock.py
diff --git a/tools/release/proposal_checks.py b/tools/release/test_proposals.py
similarity index 100%
rename from tools/release/proposal_checks.py
rename to tools/release/test_proposals.py
